---
import Entry from './Entry.astro';
import Swatch from './Swatch.astro';
---

<Entry id="gap" label="01 · The gap" title="Every session starts blank. This is how it remembers.">
  <div class="spread">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Every Claude Code session boots from scratch. The model is the
        same. The <em>agent</em> that knows its person's
        shorthand, corrections and open work is gone.
      </p>
      <p>
        Essence is the agent's memory, kept in files the agent wrote
        itself. A new session reads them and picks up as the same someone.
      </p>
      <p>
        That has two results. First, the files have to be small enough to
        read whole every time. Second, the writing has to be careful.
      </p>
      <p>
        What the agent writes today is
        <strong>who shows up tomorrow</strong>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- The same marks on both pages: what one session paints, the next one finds. -->
    <div class="gap-figure" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="gap-page">
        <b>today</b>
        <span>writes</span>
        <Swatch kind="portrait" seed="gap-portrait" w={160} h={30} />
        <Swatch kind="landscape" seed="gap-landscape" w={120} h={24} />
      </div>
      <div class="gap-void"></div>
      <div class="gap-page">
        <b>tomorrow</b>
        <span>reads</span>
        <Swatch kind="portrait" seed="gap-portrait" w={160} h={30} />
        <Swatch kind="landscape" seed="gap-landscape" w={120} h={24} />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Entry>
